{
  "id": "browser-start-command-registration-and-dispatch",
  "title": "browser.start command: registration and dispatch",
  "kind": "callpath",
  "answers": [
    "How is browser.start registered?",
    "Where is the Browser addon loaded?",
    "What key binds browser.start in console?"
  ],
  "body": "- mitmproxy/addons/browser.py:Browser.start is decorated `@command.command(\"browser.start\")`; arg `browser: str = \"chrome\"`.\n- Dispatch in start: chrome|chromium → Browser.launch_chrome; firefox → Browser.launch_firefox; else logs \"Invalid browser name.\"\n- If a browser already runs, logs \"Starting additional browser\" and appends to the list.\n- Addon instantiated in mitmproxy/addons/__init__.py:default_addons() as `browser.Browser()`.\n- Console binding: mitmproxy/tools/console/defaultkeys.py `km.add(\"B\", \"browser.start\", [\"global\"], ...)`.\n- Lifecycle: class-level lists Browser.browser (Popen) and Browser.tdir (TemporaryDirectory); Browser.done() kills processes, cleans temp dirs, resets lists.",
  "tags": [
    "browser",
    "command",
    "addon"
  ],
